      "description": "TriExport automatically splits your Multisport workout into separate swim, bike, and run activities — and uploads each one to Strava with correct heart rate, GPS, and split times intact.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n1. Complete your triathlon or brick workout as a Multisport activity on Apple Watch\n2. Open TriExport\n3. Select your workout\n4. Tap Export\n5. Upload each file to your Strava account as a manual activity\n6. Done — three clean Strava activities, properly logged\n\nWHAT YOU GET\n· Accurate split times per discipline\n· Heart rate data preserved per segment\n· GPS track per segment\n· Clean Strava activity titles\n· No manual editing, no FIT file surgery\n\nPERFECT FOR\n· Sprint, Olympic, 70.3 and full triathlon training\n· Brick workouts\n· Any multi-discipline session you want tracked separately\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nStrava's segment leaderboards, pace analysis, and weekly load stats only work correctly when activities are logged by discipline. One merged blob skews your suffer score, wrecks your run pace history, and makes your swim volume invisible. TriExport gives each discipline the data it deserves.",
